  subgraph env["One uv-managed venv — one Python, ordinary Python package deps only;\nthe same on both floors: Linux + NVIDIA and Apple Silicon"]
    app["Stream\n(stream.py: @stream functions over a StreamBuilder compile the stream's graph\nfrom @node classes, ports declared with @node.input / @node.output — hosts no node;\nmay expose ports private or public; compiled in the project's own interpreter;\nthe graph is data — one shape with what the runtime renders live — that a runtime runs)"]
    procs["Node classes\n(importable modules — imported by the stream,\ndescribed in the stream's own interpreter when a graph naming them loads, run by processor interpreters;\nnever hosted in the stream's process or the runtime process;\nthe class's import path is its identity)"]
    pkgs["Extension wheels\n(ordinary PyPI packages — Rust inside for speed, a Python node\nas the binding; depend on tatolab-stream, never on the runtime, never link the engine;\nnative internals expose handles, never streamlib internals;\none mechanism — a processor extension added by stream_builder.add that calls its own\nRust directly; no package extends the engine, each sets itself up where its nodes run,\nand an engine-grade capability enters as a built-in; first-party optional capabilities ship this way too,\nnetworking shipped first — tatolab-webrtc (tatolab.webrtc: WhipPublisher / WhepPlayer), on the encoded\nside of the codec blocks, touching no surface and no GPU;\nlive in packages/, local-linked in-repo, published to PyPI beside tatolab-stream)"]
    wheel["tatolab-stream and the lend\n(tatolab-stream (tatolab.stream): pure Python from PyPI, every stream venv installs it,\nand a stream imports, type-checks, compiles and is tested with no runtime present;\nbuilt-in nodes are classes generated from the runtime's descriptors with typed configs;\nwhat the runtime backs is declared once there as Protocols and runtime-backed functions,\nheld to both binaries by a conformance gate, so the two floors are one surface and an\nabsent capability is a closed list refused by name; no public Python name says processor;\ntatolab.runtime: the native bindings and the processor-interpreter bootstrap, built into\nthe runtime unit's lend directory beside tatolabd and tatolab — never on pip, never in a\nvenv; on macOS it carries the Vulkan loader and MoltenVK, named to the loader additively;\none version number for everything released from this repository — tatolab-stream,\nthe runtime and the first-party extensions, released together;\nthe bag codec is the one encode/decode pair\nan extension carrying a bag over its own transport reaches)"]
    helper["Processor interpreters — every Python node\n(engine exec of the stream's own venv interpreter, with the\nruntime's lend directory (holding tatolab/runtime/) prepended to PYTHONPATH;\nown interpreter, own GIL; imports the lent tatolab.runtime, not a wheel in\nits venv, beside the venv's tatolab.stream;\nrefuses to start unless that runtime is the\nparent's own engine build, id checked before\nany channel or socket opens;\nthe only placement)"]
  end

  rustapp["Rust app\n(plain cargo project)"]
  crate["streamlib crate\n(embeddable Rust library)"]
  engine["Engine runtime\n(runtime/streamlib-engine, hosted by the native tatolabd — no Python in its process;\ntoday one stream per tatolabd, started attached by tatolab run;\none runtime per machine runs many streams (decided, not yet built):\ntatolabd, owned by one user — another user's runtime is refused; one GpuContext and local API per machine — and, decided 2026-10-04, the machine's MoQ endpoint,\nwith no bundled relay; event topic, registry, interpreter,\nlogs, shutdown and interpreter table per stream; streams link freely on the machine;\nrun / run -d (kept, re-loaded on start) / stop / streams / dev; on Apple, an\nSMAppService agent inside Tatolab.app)"]
  media["Built-in media blocks\n(camera / display / MicrophoneSource / SpeakerSink — native,\nin tatolabd, handle-shaped primitives;\ncapture on one video device seam — V4L2 on Linux, AVFoundation on Apple —\neach frame carrying its capture instant on both stamps, a future stamp clamped and counted;\nthe Apple event pump on the process's first thread, present from a CAMetalLayer;\naudio backend per platform — CoreAudio AUHAL → null on Apple; on Linux dlopen'd: PipeWire → ALSA → null,\nchosen by opening not by loading; vendored SPA headers\ncompile to a shim that calls only pointers, so no audio\nlibrary enters DT_NEEDED;\ndevice-paced, conditioning on the built-ins;\ncodec blocks: H264/H265 encode+decode on one video codec backend seam —\nVulkan Video on Linux, VideoToolbox on Apple, one Annex-B wire on both —\none encode body and one decode body specialised by codec identity,\ncolour conversion on the engine's existing rgb_to_nv12 — no new RHI primitive;\nall four reach Python as generated classes like every other built-in, and the\nencoded frame has a Python cast (EncodedVideoFrame) holding no surface;\nOpus encode+decode shipped over statically linked libopus, and a pure-Rust\nfragmented Mp4Sink muxing both on every platform — one track per inbound link, named by its channel;\nJpegDecoder retired unbuilt — JPEG decode lives only in Linux MJPEG capture (decided, unbuilt) — and the next codec\nfollows the built-in criterion rather than joining this node — an encoded frame is an\nordinary bag, bitstream inline as bin beside the ordering pair and sync-point flag;\nan encoded audio packet is that convention applied to audio, cast by EncodedAudioPacket;\na decoder publishes the SPS display window, never the padded coded picture;\nVirtualCameraSink (Linux only, refused at load elsewhere; no Apple port — a Camera Extension needs a bundle): one camera per processor, created at setup and removed at teardown,\nthat any other application on the machine opens — built-in under criterion (c),\ntwo doors chosen at setup and logged: a v4l2loopback device it creates through the\nmodule's control node, YUYV written by one GPU pass through the RHI's host-pointer\nimport (cached-staging copy where the driver refuses it, imported on the rig), else a\nPipeWire Video/Source node with media.role = Camera over the same dlsym'd shim, whose\nvideo half shares the audio half's entry-point list; the loopback permission is a\none-time enable-virtual-camera the user runs, never elevated by the engine;\na built-in's type is its class's import path in tatolab.stream\n(tatolab.stream:CameraSource), never its Rust path; a config key, type or graph key\nthe runtime does not know is refused at load by name)"]
  rhi["RHI\n(accelerators optional — a stream that needs no GPU runs on a machine\nwithout one (decided, not yet built);\nvulkan/rhi + streamlib-consumer-rhi —\nthe one Vulkan RHI on both floors, MoltenVK the macOS driver;\nMetal only as handles exported from Vulkan objects;\na driver's missing capability is an absent tier refused by name)"]
  interop["Interop adapters\n(app-process Rust, per floor — Vulkan, cpu-readback, skia on both;\nVulkan↔GL and Vulkan↔CUDA on Linux, named absent on macOS)"]
  ctl["Control plane — the local API\n(api-server: HTTP / WS / MCP — engine-side;\nserved on one socket in the runtime directory only the owning user can open —\nno network address serves control, and another machine's streams are changed\non that machine (ssh) or by the control client;\nMCP through rmcp, its latest revision alone (2026-07-28): POST /mcp, and /mcp/stdio\nfor MCP hosts, which launch the CLI's mcp verb, a byte pipe to the socket (ssh for\nanother machine);\nserves the node catalog — every registered type with its derived\nconfig schema and ports — the live graph, and recipes over its tools, all in the\ngraph's words — add_node / remove_node, connect by node name and port;\ndecided, not yet built: one local API per machine, its runtime's;\nevery exposed port reachable by URL, on a\nseparate read-only listener — private and public ports on loopback, public ports on the\ntailnet through tailscale serve; decided 2026-10-04: HTTP carries only what is not real time,\nand tap and exchange leave the tool set at the sharing step)"]
  cli["CLI — the native tatolab beside tatolabd, never on pip, linking no engine\nnew / dev / run · nodes / graph / tap / logs / exchange · mcp · enable-virtual-camera\n(run / dev compile the stream in the project's venv interpreter and start tatolabd\nattached, one per stream; decided 2026-10-04: tap and exchange are deleted at the sharing step;\nnew scaffolds a GlslPixelEffect plus a numpy meter; dev / run print the\ncross-floor check's warnings and never block a start;\ndecided, not yet built: shipped with the runtime by the installer —\nrun / run -d / stop / streams / dev / mcp against the one runtime per machine)"]
  wire["Wire\n(self-describing bags between nodes —\nthe only cross-language boundary)"]

  registry["Node registry\n(one JSON per live node, inside the one engine-resolved runtime\ndirectory — on Linux XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/streamlib where that is set and non-empty,\notherwise, and on macOS always, /tmp/streamlib-<uid>, owner-only and checked\nbefore the first write — which also holds the\nsurface socket and the engine-owned iceoryx2 domain)"]
  sharing["Sharing off the machine — MoQ on the tailnet (decided 2026-10-04, not yet built):\nTatolab is a simple SDK for defining live streams as pipes and sharing them with people and agents;\nTailscale users first, and nothing Tailscale already does is built — reach, machine names,\nencryption, identity and discovery come from the tailnet; robotics is out of scope;\non one machine streams share data through shared memory; off it, real-time data travels over\nMoQ on QUIC and nothing else — the engine serves a MoQ endpoint itself on its tailnet address,\non the moq-dev line (moq-net, moq-tokio) at exact pins, and a reader subscribes to it directly;\nwith no tailnet a machine shares only with itself and through a relay — nothing is built for a plain LAN;\na machine's name is its tailnet name, read with the list of machines from Tailscale's status;\nwho reads a public port on the tailnet is Tailscale's access rules — no stream map, no peer authentication;\nthe internet edge is a relay the machine has joined, a machine setting: every public port is offered\nthere and sent only while someone subscribes; the runtime joins any relay from an address and a\ncredential, and no relay is written or bundled;\nHTTP carries only what is not real time — the listing, a read-only MCP, snapshots, small samples and\nthe viewer page — on loopback and on the tailnet through tailscale serve, which tatolabd sets up on a\nport of its own when a port first goes public, saying the one command where Tailscale refuses;\nthe viewer page ships with the first version, on the stack's own player — QUIC only, no TCP fallback;\nexposure is internal, private or public, a live map checked at the stream's edge, and a link between\nstreams is always pulled by its reader; the sharing step's details are OPEN.\nRemoved first, by one change (shipped 2026-10-05): the Zenoh runtime mesh and the MoQ extension wheel —\nuntil the sharing step nothing links one machine to another;\ntap and exchange stay until the sharing step builds the snapshot the rigs read instead"]

  ctlclient["External control client\n(decided, not yet built: an extension point —\nstreamlib runs complete without one; how it plugs in is OPEN;\nsince 2026-10-04 it pushes no stream map — what it hands the runtime beyond a\nrelay address and a credential is OPEN)"]
